PatternX - Match Historical Stock pattern with current market data

- user will input Stock and Window(15,30,60,90) days (input)
- algorithm will output the similar pattern which happens from last 10-15 years data and its match percentage and year (eg. 96.4% match , 2018)
- FFT,Sliding window 



E.g

input 
- NVIDIA
- 30 DAYS


output - percentage , window date
         96.4% , 2018(oct-1 to oct 30)


- sliding window 
- normalize 
    dxx = (dx-dy)/dy 
- fft
    Xk​=∑n=0N−1​xn​e−i2πkn/N

    FFT converts the normalized stock-price data from the time domain to the frequency domain. It decomposes a price pattern into different frequency components, where low frequencies represent broader trends and higher frequencies represent faster fluctuations.

    Cooley–Tukey FFT algorithm to efficiently generate the frequency spectrum. The magnitude of each frequency component represents its strength, producing a frequency-domain signature that can later be used to compare historical stock-price patterns.

- pattern matching 
 Return_h(k) = ((Price_(h+k) - Price_h) / Price_h) × 100

  It measures how much the stock price changed after the historical pattern.

Where:

Priceh = price at the end of the historical matched window
Price
h+k = price k days after that window
k = future period, e.g. 5, 10, 15, or 30 days
Return = percentage gain/loss

    
    



